@startuml dsd_uc2_approveCashRefund
' NewEra POS - Design sequence diagram, UC2 Handle Returns: approveCashRefund(managerID, pin, reason) (Contract 9, shared with UC5), W11
' Team D - editable source of assets/dsd_uc2_approveCashRefund.png
' Render with: java -jar plantuml.jar -charset UTF-8 -tpng assets/dsd_uc2_approveCashRefund.puml
' Participants: logical view (architecture.md 4.2). Operations: system_interfaces.md 3.3, 3.7, 4.1 to 4.3; AD-05, AD-07, AD-08, AD-09.
' Messages marked <<new>> are not in the logical view or in system_interfaces.md yet (sent to Borja for the design class diagram).
title DSD UC2 Handle Returns - approveCashRefund(managerID, pin, reason) (Contract 9, shared with UC5)
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam defaultFontSize 11
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign left
skinparam ParticipantPadding 8
skinparam BoxPadding 6
skinparam NoteBackgroundColor #FFFBE6
skinparam NoteBorderColor #B7791F
skinparam maxMessageSize 190
hide footbox
box "ui.api" #EAF2E3
  participant "ctrl:ReturnController" as C
end box
box "application" #E8EEF7
  participant "h:ReturnHandler" as H
  participant ":ManagerApproval" as MA
  participant ":PaymentMethods" as PMS
  participant "cash:CashPayment\nMethod" as PM
end box
box "domain" #FFF7E0
  participant "r:Return" as R
  participant "f:Refund" as F
  participant "rli:ReturnLineItem" as RLI
end box
box "application.interfaces" #F6EDF7
  participant ":HRSystem" as HR
  participant ":EmployeeList" as EL
  participant ":CashDrawer" as DR
  participant ":Transaction\nRepository" as TR
  participant ":ReceiptPrinter" as PRT
end box

[-> C : POST /api/returns/{returnID}/cash-approval {manager, pin, reason}
C -> H : approveCashRefund(managerID, pin, reason)
H -> R : refund()
R --> H : f
alt f is not NEEDS_APPROVAL (paid, pending or no refund)
  H --> C : NOT_WAITING_FOR_APPROVAL
  C -->[ : 409 "This refund does not need an approval"
else f waits for approval
  H -> MA : approve(managerID, pin)
  note right of MA : one class for every manager approval (price, refund, damage, AD-09);\nthe PIN is only compared, never stored, logged or shown (NFR-08)
  MA -> HR : checkEmployee(managerID, pin)
  note right of HR : the adapter applies the 5 s timeout (AD-07)
  alt HR System answers
    HR --> MA : EmployeeCheck(valid or not valid, role)
  else NOT_AVAILABLE (IR-08, FR-44)
    HR --> MA : NOT_AVAILABLE
    MA -> EL : find(managerID)
    EL --> MA : EmployeeEntry (salted hash of the PIN, role, local disable mark)
    MA -> MA : compare the hash of pin with the saved hash
  end
  alt the ID is not an active store manager, or the PIN is not correct
    MA --> H : DENIED
    H --> C : DENIED
    C -->[ : 403 "Not a store manager or wrong PIN" (the cashier can try again, no change)
  else approved
    MA --> H : manager (Employee, role StoreManager)
    H -> F : approve(manager, reason)
    note right of F : isApproved = true, approvedBy = manager, approvalReason = reason,\ntender = CASH (Contract 9). Information Expert: the Refund changes its own state.
    H -> PMS : get(CASH)
    PMS --> H : cash
    H -> PM : payOut(f.amount, employeeID) <<new>>
    PM -> DR : open(CASH_REFUND, employeeID)
    DR --> PM : OPENED (logged, IR-14)
    PM --> H : CASH_PAID
    H -> R : complete()
    loop each ReturnLineItem with condition RESELLABLE
      R -> RLI : restock()
    end
    R --> H : AccountingRecord
    H -> TR : saveCompleted(r, record)
    note right of TR : ONE database transaction, as in confirmReturn (AD-05, AD-06)
    H -> R : getReceipt()
    R --> H : receipt
    H -> PRT : print(receipt)
    PRT --> H : READY (NO_PAPER: saved, reprint later, IR-13)
    H --> C : CASH_PAID, receiptNumber
    C -->[ : 200 refund paid in cash, receipt number
  end
end

note over H, PM
  UC5 (Contract 28) uses the same steps with RentalReturnHandler and RentalReturn: ManagerApproval, Refund.approve() and the cash PaymentMethod are shared.
  The card was declined or the original payment was a check; a card refund that is still PENDING is not approved here: it is asked again with checkRefundStatus.
end note
note over H
  GRASP
  Pure Fabrication, High Cohesion: ManagerApproval holds the check of the store manager for every use case, so no handler repeats it (NFR-07).
  Information Expert: Refund records its own approval; Return restocks and builds its record.
  Polymorphism: the cash PaymentMethod opens the drawer, like every tender (AD-08).
  Protected Variations, Indirection: HRSystem and EmployeeList are interfaces; the HR System answer or the local list is the same result for the handler (IR-08, AD-04).
end note
@enduml
